From: yinjiayi <yinjiayi@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Use a valid X11 format for an empty DELETE response

XChangeProperty accepts only formats 8, 16 or 32, even for zero elements.
The original format 0 in handle_delete can provoke BadValue in the selection
owner during the retained DELETE regression. Keep the ICCCM zero-length
NULL-typed response, but describe its empty data using format 8.

Source: downstream review of the official 1.2.1 archive and Xlib/ICCCM specs.
Upstream-Status: Not submitted (no upstream writes authorized).
License: HPND-sell-variant, matching the modified upstream file.
Remove-When: The selected official release has a valid empty DELETE response.
--- a/xsel.c
+++ b/xsel.c
@@ -1465,5 +1465,5 @@
 static HandleResult
 handle_delete (Display * display, Window requestor, Atom property)
 {
-  XChangeProperty (display, requestor, property, null_atom, 0,
+  XChangeProperty (display, requestor, property, null_atom, 8,
                    PropModeReplace, NULL, 0);
